-- ccc29-xxviii-1-peace-810-02.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART XXVII, "Sureties to Keep the Peace": section 810.02 (fear of forced marriage or
-- marriage under the age of 16 years) and section 810.03 (fear of domestic violence). Layer 1: the law, objectively. The text is a plain-text
-- rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
-- The conventions of ccc29-xxviii-0-peace-810.l4 apply unchanged: "may" with an "If ... satisfied" gate answers NOTHING when the gate fails;
-- "may" with an "on application" gate answers JUST FALSE and is listed in NOTES.md; a "shall" duty whose "If" or "Where" opening fails answers
-- JUST FALSE; a stated maximum beyond its limit answers JUST FALSE ("not more than").

§ `Section 810.02 -- Fear of forced marriage or marriage under the age of 16 years`

-- 810.02(1) A person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence under paragraph 273.3(1)(d) or section 293.1 or 293.2 may lay an information before a provincial court judge.
-- src:16930 | Fear of forced marriage or marriage under age of 16 years
-- src:16931 | 810.02 (1) A person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence under paragraph 273.3(1)(d) or section 293.1 or 293.2 may lay an information before a provincial court judge.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.02(1) (src:16930-16931)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; relative-clause gate "A person who fears on reasonable grounds" (fork F-810.02-1)
GIVEN `the person fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence under paragraph 273.3(1)(d) or section 293.1 or 293.2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.02(1) the person may lay an information before a provincial court judge` MEANS
    IF `the person fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence under paragraph 273.3(1)(d) or section 293.1 or 293.2`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence under paragraph 273.3(1)(d) or section 293.1 or 293.2"

-- 810.02(2) The judge who receives the information may cause the parties to appear before a provincial court judge.
-- src:16932 | Appearances
-- src:16933 | (2) The judge who receives the information may cause the parties to appear before a provincial court judge.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.02(2) (src:16932-16933)
-- @name-test: no JUST FALSE branch; named for a power, answers NOTHING outside the scope
GIVEN `the judge receives the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.02(2) the judge may cause the parties to appear before a provincial court judge` MEANS
    IF `the judge receives the information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The judge who receives the information"

-- 810.02(3) If the provincial court judge before whom the parties appear is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the informant has reasonable grounds for the fear, the judge may order that the defendant enter into a recognizance to keep the peace and be of good behaviour for a period of not more than 12 months.
-- src:16935 | (3) If the provincial court judge before whom the parties appear is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the informant has reasonable grounds for the fear, the judge may order that the defendant enter into a recognizance to keep the peace and be of good behaviour for a period of not more than 12 months.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.02(3) (src:16935)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; gate "If ... is satisfied" (fork F-810.02-3)
GIVEN `the provincial court judge is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the informant has reasonable grounds for the fear` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.02(3) the provincial court judge may order that the defendant enter into a recognizance` MEANS
    IF `the provincial court judge is satisfied by the evidence adduced that the informant has reasonable grounds for the fear`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the provincial court judge before whom the parties appear is satisfied by the evidence adduced"

@ref Criminal Code s 810.02(3) (src:16935)
GIVEN `the period of the recognizance in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.02(3) the period of the recognizance is not more than 12 months` MEANS
    IF `the period of the recognizance in months` AT MOST 12
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of not more than 12 months"

