-- 810.02(6) The provincial court judge may add any reasonable conditions ... including conditions that (a) prohibit the defendant from making agreements or arrangements for the marriage ...; (b) prohibit ... taking steps to cause the person ... to leave the jurisdiction ...; (c) require the defendant to deposit ... any passport or any other travel document ...; (d) prohibit the defendant from communicating ... with any specified person, or refrain from going to any specified place ...; (e) require the defendant to participate in a treatment program ...; (f) require the defendant to remain within a specified geographic area ...; and (g) require the defendant to return to and remain at their place of residence at specified times.
-- src:16940 | Conditions in recognizance
-- src:16941 | (6) The provincial court judge may add any reasonable conditions to the recognizance that the judge considers desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant, including conditions that
-- src:16942 | (a) prohibit the defendant from making agreements or arrangements for the marriage, whether in or outside Canada, of the person in respect of whom it is feared that the offence will be committed;
-- src:16943 | (b) prohibit the defendant from taking steps to cause the person in respect of whom it is feared that the offence will be committed to leave the jurisdiction of the court;
-- src:16944 | (c) require the defendant to deposit, in the specified manner, any passport or any other travel document that is in their possession or control, whether or not such passport or document is in their name or in the name of any other specified person;
-- src:16945 | (d) prohibit the defendant from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any specified person, or refrain from going to any specified place, except in accordance with any specified conditions that the judge considers necessary;
-- src:16946 | (e) require the defendant to participate in a treatment program, including a family violence counselling program;
-- src:16947 | (f) require the defendant to remain within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave that area is obtained from the provincial court judge; and
-- src:16948 | (g) require the defendant to return to and remain at their place of residence at specified times.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.02(6) to s 810.02(6)(g) (src:16940-16948)
DECLARE `s 810.02(6) condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 810.02(6)(a) to prohibit the defendant from making agreements or arrangements for the marriage of the person in respect of whom it is feared that the offence will be committed`
    `s 810.02(6)(b) to prohibit the defendant from taking steps to cause that person to leave the jurisdiction of the court`
    `s 810.02(6)(c) to require the defendant to deposit any passport or any other travel document`
    `s 810.02(6)(d) to prohibit the defendant from communicating with any specified person, or to refrain from going to any specified place`
    `s 810.02(6)(e) to require the defendant to participate in a treatment program, including a family violence counselling program`
    `s 810.02(6)(f) to require the defendant to remain within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave that area is obtained from the provincial court judge`
    `s 810.02(6)(g) to require the defendant to return to and remain at their place of residence at specified times`
    `s 810.02(6) another reasonable condition`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.02(6) (src:16940-16941)
-- @name-test: no JUST FALSE branch; named for a power, answers NOTHING outside "any reasonable conditions that the judge considers desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant"
GIVEN condition IS A `s 810.02(6) condition`
      `the condition is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge considers the condition desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.02(6) the provincial court judge may add the condition to the recognizance` MEANS
    IF `the condition is reasonable` AND `the judge considers the condition desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant`
    THEN CONSIDER condition
         WHEN `s 810.02(6)(a) to prohibit the defendant from making agreements or arrangements for the marriage of the person in respect of whom it is feared that the offence will be committed` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.02(6)(b) to prohibit the defendant from taking steps to cause that person to leave the jurisdiction of the court` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.02(6)(c) to require the defendant to deposit any passport or any other travel document` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.02(6)(d) to prohibit the defendant from communicating with any specified person, or to refrain from going to any specified place` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.02(6)(e) to require the defendant to participate in a treatment program, including a family violence counselling program` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.02(6)(f) to require the defendant to remain within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave that area is obtained from the provincial court judge` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.02(6)(g) to require the defendant to return to and remain at their place of residence at specified times` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.02(6) another reasonable condition` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any reasonable conditions to the recognizance that the judge considers desirable to secure the good conduct of the defendant"

-- 810.02(7) The provincial court judge shall consider whether it is desirable ... to prohibit the defendant from possessing any firearm ... If the judge decides that it is desirable to do so, the judge shall add that condition to the recognizance and specify the period during which the condition applies.
-- src:16949 | Conditions — firearms
-- src:16950 | (7) The provincial court judge shall consider whether it is desirable, in the interests of the defendant’s safety or that of any other person, to prohibit the defendant from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all of those things. If the judge decides that it is desirable to do so, the judge shall add that condition to the recognizance and specify the period during which the condition applies.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.02(7) (src:16949-16950)
GIVEN `the information was laid under section 810.02 and the defendant is before the provincial court judge for an order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.02(7) the provincial court judge is required to consider whether a firearms prohibition is desirable` MEANS
    IF `the information was laid under section 810.02 and the defendant is before the provincial court judge for an order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provincial court judge shall consider" in proceedings under this section

@ref Criminal Code s 810.02(7) (src:16949-16950)
GIVEN `the judge decides that it is desirable to prohibit the defendant from possessing firearms and the like` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.02(7) the provincial court judge is required to add the firearms condition and specify the period during which it applies` MEANS
    IF `the judge decides that it is desirable to prohibit the defendant from possessing firearms and the like`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the judge decides that it is desirable to do so"

DECLARE `s 810.02 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 810.02(7) consider the firearms condition`
    `s 810.02(7) add the firearms condition and specify the period`
    `s 810.02(8) specify how the things and authorizations are to be surrendered`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.02(7) (src:16949-16950)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 810.02 action`
`s 810.02(7) the judge is to consider the firearms condition` MEANS
    PARTY `a provincial court judge`
    MUST `s 810.02(7) consider the firearms condition`
    HENCE `s 810.02(7) the judge is to add the firearms condition if it is desirable`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.02(7) (src:16949-16950)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 810.02 action`
`s 810.02(7) the judge is to add the firearms condition if it is desirable` MEANS
    PARTY `a provincial court judge`
    MUST `s 810.02(7) add the firearms condition and specify the period`

-- 810.02(8) If the provincial court judge adds a condition described in subsection (7) to a recognizance, the judge shall specify in the recognizance how the things ... are to be surrendered, disposed of, detained, stored or dealt with and how the authorizations, licences and registration certificates ... are to be surrendered.
