§ `Section 810.03 -- Fear of domestic violence`

-- 810.03(1) Any person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence that will cause personal injury to the intimate partner or a child of the other person, or to a child of the other person's intimate partner, may lay an information before a justice.
-- src:16955 | Fear of domestic violence
-- src:16956 | 810.03 (1) Any person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence that will cause personal injury to the intimate partner or a child of the other person, or to a child of the other person’s intimate partner, may lay an information before a justice.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.03(1) (src:16955-16956)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; relative-clause gate "Any person who fears on reasonable grounds" (fork F-810.03-1)
GIVEN `the person fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence that will cause personal injury to the intimate partner or a child of the other person, or to a child of the other person's intimate partner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.03(1) the person may lay an information before a justice` MEANS
    IF `the person fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence that will cause personal injury to the intimate partner or a child of the other person, or to a child of the other person's intimate partner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who fears on reasonable grounds that another person will commit an offence that will cause personal injury"

