-- 810.03(4) However, if the justice is also satisfied that the defendant was previously convicted of an offence in the commission of which violence was used, threatened or attempted against any intimate partner of the defendant or any child of any intimate partner or of the defendant, the justice may order the defendant to enter into the recognizance for a period of not more than two years.
-- src:16961 | Duration extended
-- src:16962 | (4) However, if the justice is also satisfied that the defendant was previously convicted of an offence in the commission of which violence was used, threatened or attempted against any intimate partner of the defendant or any child of any intimate partner or of the defendant, the justice may order the defendant to enter into the recognizance for a period of not more than two years.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.03(4) (src:16961-16962)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; gate "if the justice is also satisfied" (fork F-810.03-4)
-- Seam (PLAN section 6, [T]): section 3.01(2)(f) lists subsection 810.03(4), so "an offence in the commission of which violence was used, threatened or attempted" includes the offences section 3.01(1) lists; that answer is an input (fork F-810.03-4b).
GIVEN `the justice is also satisfied that the defendant was previously convicted of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `violence was used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the previous offence against any intimate partner of the defendant or any child of any intimate partner or of the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 3.01 the offence counts as one in which violence is used, threatened or attempted` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.03(4) the justice may order the defendant to enter into the recognizance for a longer period` MEANS
    IF `the justice is also satisfied that the defendant was previously convicted of an offence`
       AND (`violence was used, threatened or attempted in the commission of the previous offence against any intimate partner of the defendant or any child of any intimate partner or of the defendant`
            OR `s 3.01 the offence counts as one in which violence is used, threatened or attempted` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the justice is also satisfied that the defendant was previously convicted of an offence in the commission of which violence was used"

@ref Criminal Code s 810.03(4) (src:16961-16962)
GIVEN `the period of the recognizance in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.03(4) the longer period of the recognizance is not more than two years` MEANS
    IF `the period of the recognizance in months` AT MOST 24
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of not more than two years"

