-- 810.03(6) The justice may add any reasonable conditions ... including conditions requiring the defendant (a) to attend a treatment program ...; (b) to remain within a specified geographic area ...; (c) to refrain from going to any specified place or being within a specified distance of any specified place ...; (d) to wear an electronic monitoring device, with the consent of the Attorney General; (e) to abstain from communicating ... with the intimate partner, a child ... or any relative or close friend ...; (f) to abstain from the consumption of drugs ...; (g) to provide ... a sample ... on demand ...; or (h) to provide ... a sample ... at regular intervals ... Form 51.
-- src:16967 | Conditions in recognizance
-- src:16968 | (6) The justice may add any reasonable conditions to the recognizance that the justice considers desirable to ensure the good conduct of the defendant or to secure the safety and security of the intimate partner or a child of the defendant, or a child of the defendant’s intimate partner, including conditions requiring the defendant
-- src:16969 | (a) to attend a treatment program, such as an addiction treatment program or a domestic violence counselling program;
-- src:16970 | (b) to remain within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave that area is obtained from the justice;
-- src:16971 | (c) to refrain from going to any specified place or being within a specified distance of any specified place, except in accordance with any specified conditions that the justice considers necessary;
-- src:16972 | (d) to wear an electronic monitoring device, with the consent of the Attorney General;
-- src:16973 | (e) to abstain from communicating, directly or indirectly, with the intimate partner, a child of the intimate partner or of the defendant or any relative or close friend of the intimate partner, except in accordance with any specified conditions that the justice considers necessary;
-- src:16974 | (f) to abstain from the consumption of drugs — except in accordance with a medical prescription — of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance;
-- src:16975 | (g) to provide, for the purpose of analysis, a sample of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation on the demand of a peace officer, a probation officer or someone designated under paragraph 810.3(2)(a) to make a demand, at the place and time and on the day specified by the person making the demand, if that person has reasonable grounds to believe that the defendant has breached a condition of the recognizance requiring them to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance; or
-- src:16976 | (h) to provide, for the purpose of analysis, a sample of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation at regular intervals that are specified, in a notice in Form 51 served on the defendant, by a probation officer or a person designated under paragraph 810.3(2)(b) to specify them, if a condition of the recognizance requires the defendant to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.03(6) to s 810.03(6)(h) (src:16967-16976)
DECLARE `s 810.03(6) condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 810.03(6)(a) to attend a treatment program, such as an addiction treatment program or a domestic violence counselling program`
    `s 810.03(6)(b) to remain within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave that area is obtained from the justice`
    `s 810.03(6)(c) to refrain from going to any specified place or being within a specified distance of any specified place`
    `s 810.03(6)(d) to wear an electronic monitoring device`
    `s 810.03(6)(e) to abstain from communicating with the intimate partner, a child of the intimate partner or of the defendant or any relative or close friend of the intimate partner`
    `s 810.03(6)(f) to abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance`
    `s 810.03(6)(g) to provide a sample of a bodily substance on demand`
    `s 810.03(6)(h) to provide a sample of a bodily substance at regular intervals specified in a notice in Form 51`
    `s 810.03(6) another reasonable condition`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.03(6) (src:16967-16968)
-- @name-test: no JUST FALSE branch; named for a power, answers NOTHING outside "any reasonable conditions that the justice considers desirable"
GIVEN condition IS A `s 810.03(6) condition`
      `the condition is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice considers the condition desirable to ensure the good conduct of the defendant or to secure the safety and security of the intimate partner or a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General consents to an electronic monitoring device` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.03(6) the justice may add the condition to the recognizance` MEANS
    IF `the condition is reasonable` AND `the justice considers the condition desirable to ensure the good conduct of the defendant or to secure the safety and security of the intimate partner or a child`
    THEN CONSIDER condition
         WHEN `s 810.03(6)(a) to attend a treatment program, such as an addiction treatment program or a domestic violence counselling program` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.03(6)(b) to remain within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave that area is obtained from the justice` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.03(6)(c) to refrain from going to any specified place or being within a specified distance of any specified place` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.03(6)(d) to wear an electronic monitoring device` THEN IF `the Attorney General consents to an electronic monitoring device` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the consent of the Attorney General"
         WHEN `s 810.03(6)(e) to abstain from communicating with the intimate partner, a child of the intimate partner or of the defendant or any relative or close friend of the intimate partner` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.03(6)(f) to abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.03(6)(g) to provide a sample of a bodily substance on demand` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.03(6)(h) to provide a sample of a bodily substance at regular intervals specified in a notice in Form 51` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 810.03(6) another reasonable condition` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any reasonable conditions to the recognizance that the justice considers desirable"

-- 810.03(7) The justice shall consider whether it is desirable, in the interests of the intimate partner's safety or that of any other person, to prohibit the defendant from possessing any firearm ... If the justice decides that it is desirable to do so, the justice shall add that condition to the recognizance and specify the period during which the condition applies.
-- src:16977 | Conditions — firearms
-- src:16978 | (7) The justice shall consider whether it is desirable, in the interests of the intimate partner’s safety or that of any other person, to prohibit the defendant from possessing any firearm, crossbow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all of those things. If the justice decides that it is desirable to do so, the justice shall add that condition to the recognizance and specify the period during which the condition applies.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.03(7) (src:16977-16978)
GIVEN `the information was laid under section 810.03 and the defendant is before the justice for an order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.03(7) the justice is required to consider whether a firearms prohibition is desirable` MEANS
    IF `the information was laid under section 810.03 and the defendant is before the justice for an order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The justice shall consider" in proceedings under this section

@ref Criminal Code s 810.03(7) (src:16977-16978)
GIVEN `the justice decides that it is desirable to prohibit the defendant from possessing firearms and the like` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.03(7) the justice is required to add the firearms condition and specify the period during which it applies` MEANS
    IF `the justice decides that it is desirable to prohibit the defendant from possessing firearms and the like`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the justice decides that it is desirable to do so"

@ref Criminal Code s 810.03(7) (src:16977-16978)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 810.03 action`
`s 810.03(7) the justice is to consider the firearms condition` MEANS
    PARTY `a justice`
    MUST `s 810.03(7) consider the firearms condition`
    HENCE `s 810.03(7) the justice is to add the firearms condition if it is desirable`

@ref Criminal Code s 810.03(7) (src:16977-16978)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 810.03 action`
`s 810.03(7) the justice is to add the firearms condition if it is desirable` MEANS
    PARTY `a justice`
    MUST `s 810.03(7) add the firearms condition and specify the period`

-- 810.03(8) If the justice adds a condition described in subsection (7) to a recognizance, the justice shall specify in the recognizance how the things ... shall be surrendered, disposed of, detained, stored or dealt with and how the authorizations, licences and registration certificates held by the defendant shall be surrendered.
-- src:16979 | Surrender, etc.
-- src:16980 | (8) If the justice adds a condition described in subsection (7) to a recognizance, the justice shall specify in the recognizance how the things referred to in that subsection that are in the defendant’s possession shall be surrendered, disposed of, detained, stored or dealt with and how the authorizations, licences and registration certificates held by the defendant shall be surrendered.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.03(8) (src:16979-16980)
GIVEN `the justice adds a condition described in subsection (7) to a recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.03(8) the justice is required to specify in the recognizance how the things and authorizations are to be surrendered` MEANS
    IF `the justice adds a condition described in subsection (7) to a recognizance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the justice adds a condition described in subsection (7)"

@ref Criminal Code s 810.03(8) (src:16979-16980)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 810.03 action`
`s 810.03(8) the justice is to specify how the things and authorizations are to be surrendered` MEANS
    PARTY `a justice`
    MUST `s 810.03(8) specify how the things and authorizations are to be surrendered`

-- 810.03(9) If the justice does not add a condition described in subsection (7) to a recognizance, the justice shall include in the record a statement of the reasons for not adding the condition.
-- src:16981 | Reasons
-- src:16982 | (9) If the justice does not add a condition described in subsection (7) to a recognizance, the justice shall include in the record a statement of the reasons for not adding the condition.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.03(9) (src:16981-16982)
GIVEN `the justice does not add a condition described in subsection (7) to a recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.03(9) the justice is required to include in the record a statement of the reasons for not adding the condition` MEANS
    IF `the justice does not add a condition described in subsection (7) to a recognizance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the justice does not add a condition described in subsection (7)"

@ref Criminal Code s 810.03(9) (src:16981-16982)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 810.03 action`
`s 810.03(9) the justice is to include a statement of reasons in the record` MEANS
    PARTY `a justice`
    MUST `s 810.03(9) include a statement of reasons in the record`

-- 810.03(10) A justice may, on application of the Attorney General, the informant, the person on whose behalf the information is laid or the defendant, vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance.
-- src:16983 | Variance of conditions
-- src:16984 | (10) A justice may, on application of the Attorney General, the informant, the person on whose behalf the information is laid or the defendant, vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.03(10) (src:16983-16984)
-- @name-test: listed, where/when/upon kind (F-810.03-10); answers JUST FALSE when no one of the four applies
GIVEN `the Attorney General applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the informant applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person on whose behalf the information is laid applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.03(10) the justice may vary the conditions fixed in the recognizance` MEANS
    IF `the Attorney General applies` OR `the informant applies` OR `the person on whose behalf the information is laid applies` OR `the defendant applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of the Attorney General, the informant, the person on whose behalf the information is laid or the defendant"

-- 810.03(11) If the defendant makes an application under subsection (10), the justice shall, before varying any conditions, consider the safety and security needs of the person on whose behalf the information is laid.
-- src:16985 | Consideration of safety and security needs
-- src:16986 | (11) If the defendant makes an application under subsection (10), the justice shall, before varying any conditions, consider the safety and security needs of the person on whose behalf the information is laid.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.03(11) (src:16985-16986)
GIVEN `the defendant makes an application under subsection (10)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.03(11) the justice is required, before varying any conditions, to consider the safety and security needs of the person on whose behalf the information is laid` MEANS
    IF `the defendant makes an application under subsection (10)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the defendant makes an application under subsection (10)"

@ref Criminal Code s 810.03(11) (src:16985-16986)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 810.03 action`
`s 810.03(11) the justice is to consider the safety and security needs` MEANS
    PARTY `a justice`
    MUST `s 810.03(11) consider the safety and security needs before varying any conditions`

-- 810.03(12) A warrant of committal to prison for failure or refusal to enter into the recognizance under subsection (3) may be in Form 23.
-- src:16987 | Form — warrant of committal
-- src:16988 | (12) A warrant of committal to prison for failure or refusal to enter into the recognizance under subsection (3) may be in Form 23.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.03(12) (src:16987-16988)
-- @name-test: no JUST FALSE branch; named for a liberty, answers NOTHING outside the scope
GIVEN `it is a warrant of committal to prison for failure or refusal to enter into the recognizance under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.03(12) the warrant of committal may be in Form 23` MEANS
    IF `it is a warrant of committal to prison for failure or refusal to enter into the recognizance under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A warrant of committal to prison for failure or refusal to enter into the recognizance under subsection (3)"

-- 810.03(13) The provisions of this Part apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to proceedings under this section.
-- src:16989 | Provisions of this Part to apply
-- src:16990 | (13) The provisions of this Part apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to proceedings under this section.
@ref Criminal Code s 810.03(13) (src:16989-16990)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under section 810.03` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 810.03(13) the provisions of this Part apply to the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings under section 810.03`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to proceedings under this section"
